-------------------------------------------------------------------
Fri Nov 20 06:44:47 UTC 2026 - Fridrich Strba <fstrba@suse.com>

- Upgrade to version 2.0.86 Final
  * Wipe session ticket keys before freeing them (#1052)
  * Make setNpnProtos0 and setAlpnProtos0 safe on failure and
    validate the protocol list (#1029)
  * Make the narrowing of the options in getOptions explicit
    (#1048)
  * Preserve the selected credential after handshake completion
    (#1051)
  * Fail the build when a downloaded archive does not match its
    SHA-256 (#1049)
  * Use const STACK_OF(SSL_CIPHER)* for SSL_get_ciphers (#1050)
  * Reject negative sizes in SSLContext.setMaxCertList (#1047)
  * Pass the uncompressed length as jint when calling the Java
    decompress method (#1046)
  * Reject session timeouts that do not fit into 32 bits on
    BoringSSL / AWS-LC (#1045)

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Tue Nov  3 08:58:43 UTC 2026 - Fridrich Strba <fstrba@suse.com>

- Upgrade to version 2.0.85 Final
  * Fix out-of-bounds read in select_next_proto when no protocol
    matches (#1044)
  * Check for allocation failures that were previously unchecked
    (#1040)
  * Send unknown_ca when the chain was truncated and the
    TrustManager rejected the certificate (#1038)
  * Validate timeout, cache mode and cache size before narrowing
    them (#1036)
  * Don't sign-extend int options into the 64 bit SSL options
    (#1035)
  * Throw IllegalArgumentException when signing algorithm id does
    not fit into 16 bits (#1034)
  * Fix native memory leak in SSL_CTX_setup_certs when using
    BoringSSL or AWS-LC (#1031)
  * Do not discard the configured password when setCertificate(Bio)
    fails without a new one (#1030)
  * Throw NPE when null is passed to setSessionTicketKeys0 and
    setSessionIdContext (#1028)
  * Fix native memory leaks in SSLContext JNI_OnLoad (#1027)
  * Fix native memory leaks in SSLContext.setPrivateKeyMethod0
    (#1026)
  * Fix native memory leak in SSL.parseX509Chain when the BIO is
    null (#1025)
  * Support SSLContext.setKeyLogCallback with OpenSSL 1.1.1+ (#1021)
  * Update getSigAlgs to handle algorithms without combined NID
    (#1019)
  * Delete local references to Java-returned result arrays in JNI
    callbacks (#1016)
  * Fix infinite loop in musl_compat fallbacks on old glibc headers
    (#1037)
  * Preserve musl compatibility in FIPS build (#1008)
  * Update to latest netty-jni-util release (#1041)
  * Upgrade apr to 1.7.6 (#1032)

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Tue Sep 22 15:19:36 UTC 2026 - Fridrich Strba <fstrba@suse.com>

- Upgrade to version 2.0.84 Final
  * Security fixes:
    + CVE-2026-116539, GHSA-gf9q-9mg7-g5qh, bsc#1289170: Heap buffer
      overflow in tcn_write_to_bytebuffer BIO callback from
      unhandled ring buffer write index wrap (JVM crash DoS).
    + CVE-2026-116540, GHSA-mmc8-vg2v-fvvw, bsc#1289171:
      Use-after-free in ssl_tlsext_ticket_key_cb during session
      ticket key rotation with OpenSSL 3.x.
    + CVE-2026-116541, GHSA-9xr3-jwv4-r489, bsc#1289172: DoS in
      tcn_write_to_bytebuffer BIO write callback overreporting
      consumed bytes during TLS 1.3 post-handshake flights.
    + CVE-2026-116542, GHSA-2784-hxmm-4hgf, bsc#1289173: SNI
      hostname spoofing via embedded NUL bytes and overlong UTF-8
      encodings in JNI NewStringUTF decoding.

